  cold misses:  the first encode on a fresh context, every width still 1.
  warm misses:  the second encode, widths carrying what the first learned. A
                server is in this state; the cold column is a startup cost paid
                once per context.
  grows:        buffer reallocations. The harness gives the context a buffer big
                enough for the payload, so a nonzero grow here is a defect in the
                sizing and not a property of the codec.

